  "narrative": "The new results strongly support that the major associations are not produced by the particular co-mutation restrictions used in H15-H17. For H15, SMARCA4 loss remains associated with much stronger dependency when KEAP1 and STK11 are absent: signed estimate +0.801, interval +0.731 to +0.872, fully above the 0.15-unit threshold. H16 similarly shows that KEAP1 loss remains associated with much weaker dependency when SMARCA4 and STK11 are absent: signed estimate +0.821, interval +0.752 to +0.890. H17 shows TP53 loss remains associated with weaker dependency when KEAP1 and SMARCA4 are absent: signed estimate +0.402, interval +0.302 to +0.502. These restricted estimates are close to the corresponding marginal effects, so in this dataset the SMARCA4, KEAP1, and TP53 associations appear relatively robust to major co-alteration confounding, though not fully free of residual confounding. I accept all three; H16 is kept active for independent validation because it is both strong and context-defining. The added predictor screen is mostly negative for the pre-registered directions. ARID1A and MTAP loss show no meaningful stronger-dependency effect. CDKN2A loss is borderline in the expected direction: signed estimate +0.141, interval +0.062 to +0.220, but the point estimate falls below the 0.15-unit threshold and the interval is not wholly above threshold, so I reject the claim rather than accept a marginal practical effect. PTEN loss was claimed in the weaker-dependency direction, but the signed estimate is negative and precise, indicating the opposite raw pattern: PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency in this dataset. The original claim is therefore rejected, and I register a post-hoc reversed PTEN claim plus context restrictions. RB1 loss and SMAD4 loss do not support the registered directions. The subtype-interaction results also clarify context: KEAP1 and TP53 do not differ meaningfully by adenocarcinoma subtype, but SMARCA4 does: the claimed direction is rejected, and the signed interaction is negative with an interval excluding the claimed positive side, implying that the SMARCA4 stronger-dependency association is actually smaller in adenocarcinoma than in the subtype complement. This is post-hoc context discovery, not causal evidence. I register reversed SMARCA4 subtype-interaction and subtype-main claims, as well as PTEN context claims, for follow-up. Given the one-validation limit, I request validation of H16 rather than H14/H13, because validating the co-mutation-restricted KEAP1 effect directly tests independence from the strongest confounding structures. All conclusions remain dataset-specific association statements, not causal or generalizable claims.",
  "research_notes": "Current dataset-specific accepted map: H5 SMARCA4 loss -> much stronger dependency, validated. H13 TP53 loss -> weaker dependency, active. H14 KEAP1 loss -> weaker dependency, active. H15 SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency when KEAP1/STK11 absent: signed +0.801 interval +0.731 to +0.872, accepted closed. H16 KEAP1 loss weaker dependency when SMARCA4/STK11 absent: signed +0.821 interval +0.752 to +0.890, accepted active, independent validation requested. H17 TP53 loss weaker dependency when KEAP1/SMARCA4 absent: signed +0.402 interval +0.302 to +0.502, accepted closed. Negative/closed in claimed directions: H1 KRAS negative, H2 TP53 negative, H3 STK11 negative, H4 KEAP1 negative, H6 MYC amp negative, H7 marker D negative, H8 marker E negative, H9 Avana negative, H10 KRAS adenocarcinoma interaction, H11 KEAP1-STK11 interaction, H12 marker D-by-signature-B interaction, H19 ARID1A negative, H20 MTAP negative, H21 CDKN2A negative borderline but estimate 0.141 < threshold, H22 PTEN weaker, H23 RB1 negative, H24 SMAD4 weaker, H27 SMARCA4 adenocarcinoma stronger-dependency interaction, H28 KEAP1 subtype interaction, H29 TP53 subtype interaction. Important post-hoc signals: PTEN loss appears associated with stronger dependency (raw negative), because original direction +1 yielded signed -0.227 interval -0.323 to -0.131; new reversed PTEN main/context claims registered. SMARCA4 subtype interaction appears opposite to pre-registered direction: original signed -0.211 interval -0.359 to -0.063, so raw interaction positive; SMARCA4 association is likely weaker in adenocarcinoma than complement. New reversed subtype interaction and adenocarcinoma-main claims registered. Pending analyses: H18 marker F, H25 BRCA2 loss, H26 MSI-high, H30 SMARCA4 when ARID1A absent, H31 matched RNA/DNA technical effect. Next analysis priorities: H30 and new PTEN/CDKN2A context claims, new SMARCA4 subtype refinement, H31 technical confounding check, then broad pending marker/alteration claims. Interpretation remains association-only in supplied dataset; avoid mechanism/causality and generalization unless validation and external data support.",
