e rather than closed because the claim is new, arose from a direction reversal, and should be strengthened by independent validation and low-mask context tests.  Overall supported findings in the supplied dataset are now: SMARCA4 loss is strongly associated with stronger dependency broadly and in selected contexts; KEAP1 loss is strongly associated with weaker dependency broadly and in several contexts, including within SMARCA4-loss cells; TP53 loss is associated with weaker dependency broadly and also within KEAP1-loss and SMARCA4-loss backgrounds; and MSI-high status is now accepted as associated with much stronger dependency. PTEN loss remains a secondary, context-dependent stronger-dependency signal, accepted only in selected low-mask or co-mutation-restricted backgrounds, especially TP53-intact cells, TP53/KEAP1-intact cells, triple-intact cells, and KEAP1-loss cells. Broad PTEN remains borderline and is not accepted as a first-tier predictor. Negative or unsupported associations remain broad for KRAS mutation, STK11 loss, MYC amplification, PIK3CA mutation, ARID1A loss, MTAP loss, RB1 loss, SMAD4 loss, research markers D/E/F, APC mutation, NF1 loss, BRCA2 loss, BRAF mutation, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, matched-omics completeness, Avana library status, high media serum, and several interaction tests. The KY library raw contrast is in the opposite direction but remains below threshold, so it is not accepted. Borderline unresolved signals include CDKN2A loss in triple-intact contexts, PTEN loss among KEAP1-intact cells, PTEN loss among adenocarcinoma cells, PTEN loss among adenocarcinoma TP53-intact cells, and the SMARCA4-by-adenocarcinoma interaction claim H35.  The most informative next analysis is independent validation of H80 if validation capacity permits, followed by low-mask MSI-high context tests. I registered MSI-high comparisons within TP53-intact, KEAP1-intact, SMARCA4-intact, and TP53/KEAP1-intact cells to ask whether the very large MSI-high stronger-dependency association persists when opposing or same-direction co-alterations are restricted. These should be judged by whether the lower bound remains above 0.15. Remaining useful completion analyses are H53 CDKN2A within TP53-loss cells, H60 SMARCA4 within STK11-loss cells, H61 KEAP1 within STK11-loss cells, and the technical untested omics/HUMANGE_CD claims if they can be analyzed with valid cells. Further retesting of the already validated central SMARCA4, KEAP1, TP53, and broad TP53 main effects would be less informative than validating and localizing MSI-high and finishing the predictor landscape.",
