ency even when combined with markers that are broadly associated with weaker dependency or with STK11 loss. H61 tests KEAP1 loss within STK11-loss cells under direction +1, where positive signed values mean KEAP1-loss cells are less negative and therefore weaker dependent. The signed estimate is +0.860, interval +0.715 to +1.005, so I accept and close this context. Together with H57, KEAP1 loss remains associated with weaker dependency even inside the strongest opposing co-mutation background.  The remaining technical claims do not support meaningful platform-availability or library effects in the claimed directions. H69 HUMANGE_CD library, H68 RNA-omics availability, and H43 DNA-omics availability all have small signed estimates below the 0.15-unit threshold and intervals spanning near-zero. Their raw directions are slightly toward stronger dependency in the exposed categories, but not meaningfully so. I reject and close these as registered claims. They do not threaten the biological associations as nuisance signals of threshold size.  The main caution is multiplicity and the fact that H80 was accepted after reversing an originally registered direction. The new context tests reduce that concern because the MSI-high effect is large and robust in multiple prespecified backgrounds, but they are not independent validation. Therefore I request independent validation of H80, the broad MSI-high stronger-dependency claim. If validation confirms, I will close H80. If validation is weak, the clean-context H83-H85 results will determine whether the broad claim should remain accepted or be downgraded. No causal or generalizability claim is being made; all conclusions are dataset-specific associations among measured predictors.",
