elated accepted claims and additional localizations can be assessed separately. H20 MTAP loss under direction -1 receives independent validation R79: signed estimate -0.019, interval -0.122 to +0.085. This is negligible, interval spans zero, and it does not support the claimed stronger-dependency direction. I keep H20 rejected and close it. Overall supported findings in the supplied dataset are: SMARCA4 loss is strongly associated with much stronger dependency broadly and across many co-mutation contexts; KEAP1 loss is strongly associated with much weaker dependency broadly and across many contexts, including within SMARCA4-loss cells; TP53 loss is associated with weaker dependency broadly and in selected loss backgrounds; MSI-high status is associated with much stronger dependency broadly and in clean low-mask contexts, now with independent validation; and PTEN loss is a secondary context-dependent stronger-dependency signal in selected low-mask or co-mutation-restricted backgrounds, especially TP53-intact cells, TP53/KEAP1-intact cells, triple-intact cells, and KEAP1-loss cells. Negative or unsupported associations remain broad for KRAS mutation, STK11 loss, MYC amplification, PIK3CA mutation, ARID1A loss, MTAP loss, RB1 loss, SMAD4 loss, research markers D/E/F, APC mutation, NF1 loss, BRCA2 loss, BRAF mutation, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, omics-availability variables, library indicators, and media serum. Borderline unresolved signals include broad PTEN loss, PTEN loss in KEAP1-intact or adenocarcinoma contexts, CDKN2A loss in triple-intact cells, the SMARCA4-by-adenocarcinoma interaction claim H35, and several MSI or central-marker context and interaction probes. The most informative next analyses are the remaining MSI localizations H81, H82, H88, and the newly proposed H94 MSI-high within TP53-loss cells, followed by PTEN localization H91 and residual context completion H53, H92, and H93.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 6 synthesis update: H80 MSI-high broad stronger-dependency claim now accepted and closed after independent validation: discovery +0.792 lower +0.676, validation +0.769 lower +0.594, both signed under direction -1. MSI-high is a robust dataset-specific association, but not causal or externally validated. H39 PTEN loss in TP53-intact remains accepted and closed with caution: discovery +0.259 lower +0.169, validation +0.262 lower +0.115; point estimate stable but validation lower dips below 0.15 threshold. Treat PTEN as secondary context-dependent, not first-tier broad. H20 MTAP loss remains rejected and closed; independent validation signed estimate is tiny and interval includes zero. Current supported predictor landscape: SMARCA4 loss strong dependency, KEAP1 loss weak dependency, TP53 loss weak dependency, MSI-high strong dependency, PTEN loss context-dependent strong dependency in selected TP53-intact/low-mask contexts. Broad PTEN, several PTEN subcontexts, CDKN2A triple-intact, SMARCA4-by-adenocarcinoma, and many interactions remain unresolved or borderline. New proposal H94 asks whether MSI-high remains associated with stronger dependency within TP53-loss cells; it may be cell-size limited, so invalidity is inconclusive. Next analyze priorities: H81 MSI in TP53-intact, H82 MSI in KEAP1-intact, H88 MSI mutation-burden interaction, H94 MSI in TP53-loss, H91 PTEN in TP53/SMARCA4-intact, H53 CDKN2A in TP53-loss, H92 KEAP1 in TP53-loss, H93 TP53 in STK11-loss. Avoid repeated validation of already confirmed broad claims; remaining validation capacity 5 is better reserved for newly robust unresolved or borderline context effects."
