  "narrative": "These new proposals are refinements and complements to the already supported core map: SMARCA4 loss strongly increases dependency, KEAP1 loss strongly reduces dependency, TP53 loss reduces dependency, MSI-high strongly increases dependency, and PTEN loss is a secondary context-dependent stronger-dependency signal. The signed convention remains: for direction -1, positive signed values indicate stronger dependency; for direction +1, positive signed values indicate weaker dependency. For interactions, positive signed values indicate the claimed modification direction. First, I propose a valid high-mutation-burden localization of MSI-high rather than another invalid MSI-by-mutation-burden interaction. Because all MSI-high cells appear to lie in the high-burden stratum in the invalid interaction tests, a mean difference within the high-burden population is the right way to test whether MSI-high remains associated with stronger dependency after restricting to comparable high-TMB cells. Second, I add focused PTEN refinements: PTEN loss in STK11-loss with TP53 intact, PTEN loss in KEAP1-loss with TP53 intact, and PTEN loss in adenocarcinoma with TP53 and SMARCA4 intact. These ask whether the secondary PTEN association is robust in important co-mutation or histological backgrounds, especially where TP53 loss and SMARCA4 loss do not confound or mask the signal. Third, I register core-by-core interaction refinements: whether TP53-loss weaker-dependency association is modified by KEAP1 loss within SMARCA4/STK11-intact cells; whether TP53-loss is modified by STK11 loss within KEAP1-intact cells; whether SMARCA4-loss stronger-dependency is modified by STK11 loss in a low-mask background; and whether TP53 loss modifies PTEN loss in a KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact background. These are useful because the broad main effects are now established, and the next scientific question is whether measured co-mutation contexts meaningfully amplify or attenuate them. Invalid interaction tests with zero cells should not be requested again; the new high-burden MSI mean difference is the informative alternative. Validation capacity remains limited, so H40 PTEN-in-KEAP1-intact should remain the leading voluntary validation target if no scheduled validation is delivered and if this exploration does not already resolve that context. H94/H95 remain accepted but active because they are small-cell MSI contexts.",
  "research_notes": "Post explore iteration 8: New proposals registered. Priority new MSI test: MSI_high within high mutation_burden (ge median), avoiding invalid zero-cell MSI-by-burden interactions. PTEN refinements: STK11-loss TP53-intact; KEAP1-loss TP53-intact; adenocarcinoma TP53/SMARCA4-intact; and PTEN-by-TP53 interaction within KEAP1/SMARCA4-intact. Core interaction refinements: TP53_loss interaction with KEAP1-loss in SMARCA4/STK11-intact (parent H38), TP53_loss interaction with STK11-loss in KEAP1-intact (parent H93), SMARCA4_loss interaction with STK11-loss in TP53/KEAP1-intact (parent H60). Keep H40 active as possible validation target if capacity remains; do not request validation of invalid H88/H96. H94/H95 accepted but active. Core broad accepted/validated map remains SMARCA4 loss stronger, KEAP1 loss weaker, TP53 loss weaker, MSI-high stronger. PTEN remains secondary context-dependent. Maintain signed-direction convention."
}

