  "narrative": "Assessment of the response deadlines and new validation evidence reinforces the core predictor map while sharpening the status of PTEN loss and confirming two null secondary leads. Under the registered signed convention, for direction -1 a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has stronger dependency; for direction +1 a positive signed estimate means the exposed group has weaker dependency.\n\nH80 broad MSI-high association is now independently confirmed. The discovery contrast was +0.792 signed dependency units (95% interval +0.676 to +0.907), and the independent validation estimate was +0.769 with adjusted interval +0.594 to +0.944. The validation lower bound is far above the 0.15-unit scientific threshold. I therefore accept and close H80 as a dataset-specific association between MSI-high status and much stronger dependency_composite. This is not a causal or generalizable biological claim.\n\nH20 MTAP loss remains unsupported. The discovery signed estimate was only +0.008 (95% interval -0.068 to +0.085), and the validation estimate was -0.019 (adjusted interval -0.123 to +0.085). Both are near zero and far below the 0.15-unit threshold in any robust sense. I reject and close H20.\n\nH40 PTEN loss in KEAP1-intact cells is now accepted based on converging discovery and independent validation. The discovery signed estimate was +0.233, interval +0.133 to +0.332; its lower bound was just below threshold. The validation estimate was larger at +0.328, and the independent adjusted interval was +0.184 to +0.471, with the lower bound above threshold. I accept and close H40. This means PTEN loss is associated with stronger dependency among KEAP1-intact cells, a large and relevant subgroup. This strengthens PTEN as a secondary context-dependent predictor, but it does not by itself establish the whole-population PTEN claim.\n\nH46 EGFR amplification is confirmed as unsupported. The discovery signed estimate was +0.092 (interval -0.014 to +0.197), and the validation estimate was +0.036 (adjusted interval -0.102 to +0.174). There is no meaningful evidence in the claimed weaker-dependency direction. I reject and close H46.\n\nOverall supported dataset-specific associations now include the four broad, independently validated effects: SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger dependency (H5), TP53 loss with much weaker dependency (H13), KEAP1 loss with much weaker dependency (H14), and MSI-high status with much stronger dependency (H80). PTEN loss is best characterized as a secondary predictor: it is accepted in several restricted or biologically informative backgrounds, including TP53-intact contexts, triple-intact molecular backgrounds, KEAP1-loss TP53-intact cells, TP53/SMARCA4-intact cells, and now KEAP1-intact cells. However, the broad unadjusted PTEN claim H32 remains unresolved because its discovery lower bound, +0.131, was below the 0.15-unit threshold. I have set H32 active because independent validation of broad PTEN loss is now the most informative remaining validation target: it would tell us whether PTEN loss should be described as a broadly supported secondary association or only as a collection of context-specific accepted localizations.\n\nThe negative findings remain broad and useful. Broad associations were not supported for KRAS mutation, STK11 loss overall, MYC amplification, PIK3CA mutation, ARID1A loss, MTAP loss, RB1 loss, SMAD4 loss, research markers D/E/F, APC mutation, NF1 loss, BRCA2 loss, BRAF mutation, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, omics-availability variables, CRISPR library indicators, or media serum. Interaction evidence generally failed to show threshold-sized co-mutation or transcriptomic-state modification of the core effects, although some interactions remain underpowered rather than definitively absent.\n\nThe main unresolved uncertainties are: broad PTEN loss H32; PTEN loss in STK11-loss backgrounds H97/H101; the suggestive TP53-by-STK11 interaction H105; small-cell MSI-high contexts H94/H95; borderline PTEN in adenocarcinoma low-mask background H103; and the remaining untested exploratory interaction claims H74-H79. The most informative next analysis is therefore focused PTEN consolidation, especially the proposed PTEN-loss comparison in STK11-intact cells, together with the already active untested interaction panel and validation follow-up for H32 or H103 depending on new results. All conclusions remain associations measured in this supplied dataset and should not be interpreted as causal mechanisms or externally generalizable biological rules.",
