  "narrative": "This synthesis evaluates the three pending evidence deadlines and updates the dataset-specific conclusion about PTEN loss. All numbers below are already signed to the registered hypothesis direction: for main effects with direction -1, a positive estimate means stronger dependency in the exposed group; for direction +1, a positive estimate means weaker dependency. H40 tests PTEN loss among KEAP1-intact cells in the stronger-dependency direction. Discovery gave +0.233 (95% interval +0.133 to +0.332; R35), and independent validation gave a larger adjusted estimate +0.328 with adjusted lower bound +0.184 (R105). Because the point estimate and the independent validation lower bound both exceed the 0.15-unit threshold, I accept and close H40. This provides a robust, dataset-specific association between PTEN loss and stronger dependency in the KEAP1-intact background, without claiming causality or external generalizability. H46 tests EGFR amplification in the weaker-dependency direction. Discovery gave a small and imprecise +0.092 (-0.014 to +0.197; R60), and independent validation gave +0.036 (-0.102 to +0.174; R106). The validation estimate is far below threshold and the adjusted interval is incompatible with a threshold-sized effect. I therefore reject and close H46 as unsupported: EGFR amplification is not a meaningful positive predictor of weaker dependency_composite in this supplied dataset. H111 tests PTEN loss among cells that are STK11-intact and TP53-intact, the main unresolved broad-context PTEN hypothesis. Discovery gave +0.235 with lower bound +0.136 (R109), and independent validation gave +0.263 with adjusted lower bound +0.105 (R130). The direction is concordant and both point estimates are above the threshold, but neither interval provides a lower bound above the 0.15-unit threshold; in particular, the independent validation interval remains compatible with a smaller-than-threshold effect. Therefore I keep H111 unresolved and deferred rather than accept it. This failure of independent interval confirmation is important: it argues against upgrading PTEN loss to a broad, uniformly threshold-sized secondary predictor in common low-mask backgrounds. It does not overturn the already accepted context-specific PTEN associations, because those contexts have their own discovery or validation evidence, but it supports interpreting PTEN loss as a context-dependent secondary predictor rather than a broadly robust main effect. The current supported dataset-specific map remains: SMARCA4 loss is associated with much stronger dependency_composite (H5 and related accepted contexts), TP53 loss with much weaker dependency_composite (H13 and related accepted contexts), KEAP1 loss with much weaker dependency_composite (H14 and related accepted contexts), and MSI-high status with much stronger dependency_composite (H80 and related accepted contexts, including adenocarcinoma-restricted H109). PTEN loss is supported as a secondary association in several measured backgrounds, including TP53-intact cells, KEAP1-intact cells, TP53/KEAP1-intact cells, TP53/SMARCA4-intact cells, triple-intact TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 cells, KEAP1-loss TP53-intact cells, and an adenocarcinoma TP53/SMARCA4-intact background. The broad unadjusted PTEN claim remains suggestive but not robust, because H32 and several lower-confidence PTEN context claims have lower confidence bounds at or below the threshold. Negative findings are broad: KRAS mutation, STK11 loss overall, MYC amplification, PIK3CA mutation, ARID1A loss, MTAP loss, RB1 loss, SMAD4 loss, NF1 loss, BRCA2 loss, BRAF mutation, EGFR amplification including independent validation, ERBB2 amplification, APC mutation, research markers D/E/F, omics-availability indicators, CRISPR library indicators, media-serum level, and batch_a versus batch_b diagnostics did not show robust threshold-sized associations in the claimed direction. Most tested interactions were also unsupported or insufficient, including lineage-subtype, growth-rate, mutation-burden, screen-quality, Wnt-activity, aneuploidy, low-9p21, hypoxia, stemness, and MYC-expression context tests. Some negative conclusions are absence of evidence rather than proof of exact nullity, especially in small cells. Remaining unresolved issues include broad PTEN loss, PTEN in STK11-intact backgrounds including H108/H110/H111/H117-H119, PTEN in STK11-loss backgrounds H97/H101, selected CDKN2A contexts, TP53-by-STK11 interaction H105, small-sample MSI-high subgroups, and exploratory interactions such as H78. Given the failed H111 validation, the most informative next analysis is not another broad PTEN claim. If the remaining voluntary validation request is used, it is better spent on a well-powered accepted or near-accepted low-mask PTEN context such as H58, PTEN loss in TP53-intact KEAP1-intact cells, or H33, PTEN loss in triple-intact TP53/KEAP1/SMARCA4 cells, to strengthen the contextual PTEN map. Otherwise, a focused follow-up on PTEN in STK11-loss backgrounds H97/H101 or a pre-specified aggregation of low-mask contexts would be more useful than accepting H32 or H111. All conclusions remain associations in the supplied dataset, not causal mechanisms or externally generalizable rules.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 10 synthesis after validation responses. H40 PTEN loss in KEAP1-intact cells is accepted and closed: discovery R35 +0.233 (95% +0.133 to +0.332), independent validation R105 +0.328 (adjusted +0.184 to +0.471); robust dataset-specific stronger-dependency context. H46 EGFR amplification is rejected and closed: discovery R60 +0.092 (-0.014 to +0.197), validation R106 +0.036 (adjusted -0.102 to +0.174); no threshold-sized weaker-dependency effect. H111 PTEN loss in STK11-intact TP53-intact cells remains unresolved and deferred: discovery R109 +0.235 (+0.136 to +0.334), validation R130 +0.263 (adjusted +0.105 to +0.421); point estimates above threshold but independent validation lower bound below threshold. This weakens broad PTEN upgrade and supports context-dependent PTEN interpretation. Current accepted core associations: SMARCA4 loss stronger dependency; TP53 loss weaker dependency; KEAP1 loss weaker dependency; MSI-high stronger dependency; all independent validation lower bounds exceed 0.15. Accepted PTEN contexts include H40 validated, H39 TP53-intact, H33 triple-intact, H58 TP53/KEAP1-intact, H91 TP53/SMARCA4-intact, H103 adenocarcinoma TP53/SMARCA4-intact, H51/H102 KEAP1-loss TP53-intact, among others, but broad H32 remains unresolved because H32 discovery +0.227 lower +0.131 and validation +0.200 adjusted lower +0.048. Next priority: if validation is available, validate a robust low-mask PTEN context such as H58 (R49 +0.255 lower +0.165) or H33 (R29 +0.252 lower +0.169), rather than broad H32 or H111. Alternative informative PTEN follow-up: focused PTEN in STK11-loss contexts H97/H101 with careful small-sample interpretation. Do not accept H108/H110/H117/H118/H119 or H32 as broad PTEN effects on current evidence. All claims remain dataset-specific associations, not causal or generalizable biological mechanisms."
