ith stronger dependency (+0.791, lower +0.636; H195/R203); TP53 loss is associated with weaker dependency (+0.676, lower +0.443; H196/R204); and KEAP1 loss is associated with weaker dependency (+0.901, lower +0.725; H197/R205). I accept these as context-persistence results, not formal effect-modification or causal claims. They are marginal within-stratum comparisons and may be influenced by correlated co-mutations or screen features, but their lower bounds are far above the effect-size threshold.\n\nIndependent validation is not possible because no new validation requests remain, and none are needed to change the status of these context results: the overall SMARCA4, TP53, KEAP1, and MSI-high claims already have prior independent validation, while these new analyses only test whether the associations persist in specified dataset contexts. I close these investigations because further subgroup mining would add multiplicity risk, especially for PTEN and marginal MYC contexts, without additional confirmatory capacity.",
