aker (R198), KEAP1 loss weaker (R200), and MSI-high stronger (R201); within MYC-amplification cells, SMARCA4 loss remained stronger (R203), TP53 loss weaker (R204), and KEAP1 loss weaker (R205). These are context-presence tests, not formal effect-modification claims. Negative findings are broad: KRAS mutation, STK11 main effect, MYC amplification main effect, PIK3CA mutation, ARID1A main effect, MTAP overall and MTAP in CDKN2A-loss cells, RB1 loss, SMAD4 loss, NF1 loss, BRCA2 loss, BRAF V600E, EGFR amplification, ERBB2 amplification, APC mutation, research markers D, E, and F, omics-availability indicators, CRISPR-library main effects, media-serum main-effect contrasts, screen batch, sex, and most formal interaction tests did not reach the 0.15 threshold in the claimed direction. The constructed-signature interaction screen mostly failed to support threshold-robust modifiers except H207; signature-A modifiers for SMARCA4, KEAP1, and MSI-high were rejected, signature-B SMARCA4 was rejected, and signature-C SMARCA4 remained unresolved but below threshold. Unresolved uncertainty is concentrated in low-power or repeatedly searched contexts: overall PTEN loss and key PTEN contexts H32, H111, and H124 remain borderline; low-power TP53-loss contexts H148, H151, H166, and H172 remain unresolved; several MYC amplification expression or copy-number contexts remain unresolved; KEAP1 interaction by adherent growth, CDKN2A secondary contexts, and H203 remain unresolved. Closing these was a multiplicity and resource decision, not proof of null. If confirmatory capacity were available, the most informative next analyses would be targeted independent validation of borderline PTEN contexts H111 and H124, plus overall PTEN H32, and low-power TP53 contexts H148, H151, H166, and H172; a pre-specified joint assessment of the core SMARCA4, TP53, KEAP1, and MSI-high associations with strict multiplicity control would be preferable to further arbitrary marker or subgroup mining.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 18 synthesis complete. No new validation/deadline; validation budget exhausted; assessments_due empty. Accepted core remains: H5 SMARCA4 loss stronger (R5, R13), H13 TP53 loss weaker (R2, R39), H14 KEAP1 loss weaker (R4, R92), H80 MSI-high stronger (R56, R78). Accepted constructed-assay interaction: H207 TP53 loss by high research_signature_A opposite direction (R208), dataset-specific only. PTEN loss is secondary/context-dependent; overall and many borderline contexts remain unresolved (H32, H111, H124). Broad negative list includes KRAS, STK11 main, MYC amp main, PIK3CA, ARID1A, MTAP, RB1, SMAD4, NF1, BRCA2, BRAF, EGFR, ERBB2, APC, markers, omics, libraries, serum main, batch, sex, most interactions. Next, if capacity exists: targeted validation of PTEN borderline contexts and low-power TP53 contexts; pre-specified joint core assessment; avoid further arbitrary marker mining."
}

