  "narrative": "No assessments are due and the voluntary validation budget is exhausted, so this explore stage registers discovery hypotheses and closes H207 as an accepted but dataset-specific constructed-assay interaction. The main scientific need now is to test the core associations in more genetically isolated backgrounds and to ask whether a biologically motivated untested RNA marker, SLFN11, modifies those core associations. The four mean_difference proposals test SMARCA4 loss, TP53 loss, KEAP1 loss, and MSI-high status while excluding the other three accepted core predictors and STK11 loss. These are refinements of the core map, not new biological pathways: expected directions are the same as in the accepted core claims because the goal is to assess whether each robust association persists when co-occurring accepted drivers are absent. For SMARCA4 loss and MSI-high, the anticipated raw exposed-minus-comparator contrast is negative because more negative dependency_composite means stronger dependency; for TP53 loss and KEAP1 loss, the anticipated raw contrast is positive because those losses are associated with weaker dependency in this dataset. The four interaction proposals test whether high SLFN11 expression, above the observed median, amplifies the core effects. SLFN11 is a plausible DNA-damage and replication-stress marker, so if it marks biologically relevant stress states, it could magnify SMARCA4-loss and MSI-high stronger-dependency contrasts and magnify the TP53-loss and KEAP1-loss weaker-dependency contrasts. Plausible alternatives are no effect modification, attenuation of the core effect, or an opposite modification. I avoid further PTEN-loss or arbitrary signature-marker subgroup mining because PTEN has already been examined across many contexts, several lower bounds remain near but below threshold, and no confirmatory validation capacity remains. Future appraisal will accept only when the signed 95% lower bound exceeds +0.15 composite dependency-score units in the claimed direction; near-threshold findings will remain unresolved.",
  "research_notes": "Iteration 19 explore. No assessments due; validation budget exhausted. Accepted core remains: SMARCA4 loss stronger composite dependency (H5), TP53 loss weaker (H13), KEAP1 loss weaker (H14), MSI-high stronger (H80). H207 TP53-loss by high research_signature_A is accepted and now closed as a dataset-specific constructed-assay interaction, not external biology. New registered claims are of two kinds. First, isolated-core background tests: each core predictor is evaluated while excluding the other three accepted core predictors and STK11 loss. These should clarify whether accepted effects persist in genetically cleaner backgrounds and reduce confounding by co-occurring robust drivers. Second, four median-split SLFN11 interaction tests ask whether high SLFN11 amplifies the core contrasts: expected SMARCA4/MSI stronger and TP53/KEAP1 weaker in high SLFN11. PTEN and constructed signatures are not further mined because of extensive prior testing and no validation budget. Interpretation remains dataset-specific association, not causality or generalizability. Acceptance rule: signed lower 95% bound > +0.15 composite dependency-score units."
}

