  "narrative": "The new evidence primarily supports persistence of the core dependency-composite associations in transcript-expression states, while not supporting broad claimed effect modification by an AXL-high state. I evaluated each signed estimate against the outcome threshold of 0.15 composite dependency-score units, with the signed lower bound needed to clear that threshold. For H216 (R223), the SMARCA4-loss interaction with AXL-high status was small and imprecise: +0.070, 95% interval [-0.080, +0.221]. It does not support claimed effect modification. For H217 (R224), the claimed positive TP53-loss interaction was opposite the claimed direction: signed estimate -0.311, interval [-0.539, -0.083]. I reject the original positive-direction claim. I do not immediately adopt a reversed reversal claim: if the direction were reversed, the signed lower bound would only be +0.083, which does not clear the 0.15 threshold, and this was one of several post hoc interaction screens, so multiplicity caution is appropriate. H218 (R225) was small and imprecise for KEAP1-loss modification by AXL-high status: +0.033, interval [-0.114, +0.179]. These three AXL interaction tests are closed as not supporting the claimed effect modification. The AXL-high mean-difference test for MSI-high (H219/R226) nevertheless shows a clearly threshold-exceeding association: +0.722, lower bound +0.482, with exposed n=30. The sample is small in the exposed cell but above the 20-cell minimum, so I accept it as a dataset-specific persistence finding, not independent validation or a causal claim. In ASCL2-high top-quartile cells, all four core contrasts persist with strong lower bounds: SMARCA4-loss H220/R227 lower +0.632, TP53-loss H221/R228 lower +0.333, KEAP1-loss H222/R229 lower +0.631, and MSI-high H223/R230 lower +0.433. These acceptances strengthen the dataset-specific association map but remain subgroup associations in overlapping populations, not independent replicates. The IFN-gamma-signature-high MSI-high contrast H224/R231 is also threshold-supported: +0.817, lower +0.649. This supports persistence of MSI-high stronger dependency in an immune-signature-high context, but it does not establish immune causality. The refined research_signature_A TP53 interaction H225/R232 remains threshold-supported at the 75th percentile: +0.526, lower +0.306, though it should continue to be described as a constructed-assay statistical interaction, not biology. The PTEN-loss refinements H226/R233 and H227/R234 are scientifically suggestive but do not meet the strict lower-bound threshold: +0.224, lower +0.132 and +0.239, lower +0.133, respectively. I leave them unresolved rather than accepting, but I do not reject them, because the point estimates exceed the threshold and the intervals are compatible with effects just above threshold. These near-threshold contexts are consistent with PTEN-loss being a secondary, context-dependent association rather than a uniform overall effect; they do not override the stronger accepted PTEN findings in more restrictively defined non-MSI, non-KEAP1, non-SMARCA4, often TP53-wild-type or lineage-restricted subsets. No validation request is made because no new voluntary validation capacity remains.",
